{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2ContentTranspose","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC2ContentTranspose","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIContentDecomposition"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqHooks_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqHooks_conj","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2ContentTranspose.lean#L101-L121","doc":"**C2, Σ-level (hook moment): the squared-hook sum is transpose-invariant.**\n`Σ_c h_c² (λ') = Σ_c h_c² (λ)`.  The hook is transpose-symmetric (`h_λ(i,j) = h_{λ'}(j,i)`): the\nconjugate's hook at `(r,c)` is `(colLen l r − c) + (λ_c − r) − 1`, equal — commuting arm and leg —\nto `l`'s hook at `(c,r)`; `colLen_conj` supplies the leg and `cell_fubini` matches the cell sets.\nThis is the moment that feeds `d_q(λ)` and thus `W_λ = W_{λ'}` (C2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.colLen_conj","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2ContentTranspose.lean#L86-L99","doc":"**Column-length involution.** The `c`-th column length of the conjugate is the `c`-th part of\n`l`: `colLen (conj l) c = λ_c`.  Proof: `colLen (conj l) c = #{r < λ_1 : c < colLen l r}`\n(`colLen_eq_indicator_sum` + `conj_getD`), then `c < colLen l r ↔ r < λ_c` (`colLen_duality`), and\n`#{r < λ_1 : r < λ_c} = min λ_1 λ_c = λ_c` (`sum_indicator_lt_eq_min` + `getD_le_headD`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqContents_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.sumSqContents_conj","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2ContentTranspose.lean#L55-L76","doc":"**C2, Σ-level (content moment): the squared-content sum is transpose-invariant.**\n`Σ_{c ∈ λ'} c(c)² = Σ_{c ∈ λ} c(c)²` for any weakly-decreasing partition.  Content negates under\ntranspose (`c(i,j) = j − i ↦ i − j`); squaring kills the sign, so the per-cell summand is preserved,\nand `cell_fubini` (the column-length duality of `IdentityIContentDecomposition`) matches the\nrow-indexed cells of `λ` with the column-indexed cells of `λ'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conj_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conj_getD","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2ContentTranspose.lean#L49-L53","doc":"Row `j` of the conjugate is the `j`-th column length (for `j` a genuine column). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conj_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conj_length","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2ContentTranspose.lean#L45-L47","doc":"The conjugate has one row per column of `l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.conj","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneC2ContentTranspose.lean#L40-L43","doc":"**Transpose (conjugate) of a partition** in the `List ℕ` model: row `j` of the conjugate is the\n`j`-th column length `colLen l j`, for `j` ranging over the columns `[0, λ_1)`.  For a\nweakly-decreasing `l` this coincides with `Partition.conjugate l`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}